TI  - Reducing Cardiovascular Side Effects of DMT Using Beta-Blockers
T2  - ACS MEDICINAL CHEMISTRY LETTERS
M3  - Editorial Material
AB  - DMT induces rapid antidepressant effects, but acute sympathomimetic side effects, particularly hypertension and tachycardia, limit its use. This study describes coformulations with short-acting beta-blockers or nitrates, matched to DMT's pharmacokinetics, to mitigate peripheral cardiovascular risks without compromising central therapeutic action, facilitating safer psychedelic therapy in vulnerable populations.
